  "kind": "movement",
  "title": "Rise of Confucianism",
  "summary": "Confucianism grew from the teachings of Confucius (traditionally 551–479 BCE), who was born in the domain of Zou, in modern Shandong. It developed in 6th-century BCE China and taught that a moral code and ritual led to a productive and peaceful life, with virtues including benevolence, righteousness and filial piety. Its classic texts became foundational to Chinese culture after it was made the state philosophy during the Han dynasty (202 BCE–220 CE).",
